    },
    "アフター, 後日談, その後 … The wording in the name is kept as the volume you see. The number it sorts by is the last volume of that series plus one; compilations and side stories, which sit at the offset, are not counted as part of the numbering." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "アフター, 後日談, その後 … The wording in the name is kept as the volume you see. The number it sorts by is the last volume of that series plus one; compilations and side stories, which sit at the offset, are not counted as part of the numbering."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "アフター、後日談、その後 … 名前に書いてある表記が、そのまま巻数(表示用)になります。並べる数は、そのシリーズの最後の巻に 1 を足した数です。オフセットで後ろに置いてある総集編・番外編は、ナンバリングには数えません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "に → 2, さん → 3, ふたつ → 2, みっかめ → 3 … Some names spell the number out in kana on purpose, either read aloud or counted. The word is kept as the volume you see; the number on the right is the one it sorts by. It is only read when the word stands on its own, so “にっこり” is left alone." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "に → 2, さん → 3, ふたつ → 2, みっかめ → 3 … Some names spell the number out in kana on purpose, either read aloud or counted. The word is kept as the volume you see; the number on the right is the one it sorts by. It is only read when the word stands on its own, so “にっこり” is left alone."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "に → 2、さん → 3、ふたつ → 2、みっかめ → 3 … わざとかなで数を書く名前があります(読み方でも、数え方でも)。巻数(表示)は書いてある語のまま、並べる数は右の数字です。語がひとまとまりで書かれているときだけ読むので、「にっこり」は読みません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "の, と, は, に. When what follows the series name with no separator starts with one of these, it is not shown as the volume" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "の, と, は, に. When what follows the series name with no separator starts with one of these, it is not shown as the volume"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "の、と、は、に。シリーズ名のあとに区切りなしで続く残りがこれで始まるなら、巻数(表示)にしません"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "壱 to 玖 (the old way of writing 一 to 九, with both 漆 and 柒 for seven), the traditional forms 壹 貳 參, and the ordinary numerals 一 to 九. “X 弐” and “X 四” are volumes 2 and 4. Take out the ones your titles use as words." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "壱 to 玖 (the old way of writing 一 to 九, with both 漆 and 柒 for seven), the traditional forms 壹 貳 參, and the ordinary numerals 一 to 九. “X 弐” and “X 四” are volumes 2 and 4. Take out the ones your titles use as words."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "壱〜玖(一〜九の大字。七は漆と柒の両方)、旧字体の壹・貳・參、ふつうの漢数字の一〜九。「X 弐」「X 四」はそれぞれ 2 巻・4 巻です。題名で言葉として使う字があれば外してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "巻, 話, 号 …" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "巻, 話, 号 …"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "巻・話・号 …"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "version" : "1.1"
